KUBERNETES MANIFEST NOTES – EASY MEMORY VERSION
==============================================

Every Kubernetes YAML has only 4 main sections:

1. apiVersion:
2. kind:
3. metadata:
4. spec:

If you remember these 4, you can write ANY manifest.

------------------------------------------------------------
1. POD MANIFEST (Basic building block)
------------------------------------------------------------
Structure:
- kind: Pod
- spec has containers

Template:
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: mypod
spec:
  containers:
    - name: mycontainer
      image: nginx

MEMORY TRICK:
Pod = containers list

------------------------------------------------------------
2. SERVICE MANIFEST (ClusterIP, NodePort, LoadBalancer)
------------------------------------------------------------
Structure:
- kind: Service
- spec has: type + ports + selector

Template:
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: myservice
spec:
  type: ClusterIP        # or NodePort / LoadBalancer
  selector:
    app: myapp
  ports:
    - port: 80
      targetPort: 8080
      # nodePort: 30080 (only for NodePort)

MEMORY TRICK:
Service = ports + selector

------------------------------------------------------------
3. REPLICATIONCONTROLLER (RC)
------------------------------------------------------------
Structure:
- spec: replicas + selector + template (Pod)

Template:
apiVersion: v1
kind: ReplicationController
metadata:
  name: myrc
spec:
  replicas: 3
  selector:
    app: myapp
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: myapp
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: nginx
          image: nginx

MEMORY TRICK:
RC = selector + template

------------------------------------------------------------
4. REPLICASET (RS)
------------------------------------------------------------
Same as RC but:
- apiVersion = apps/v1
- selector uses matchLabels

Template:
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: ReplicaSet
metadata:
  name: myrs
spec:
  replicas: 3
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: myapp
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: myapp
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: nginx
          image: nginx

MEMORY TRICK:
ReplicaSet = RC but with matchLabels

------------------------------------------------------------
5. DEPLOYMENT (Most used in real world)
------------------------------------------------------------
Structure:
- spec: replicas + selector + template (Pod)

Template:
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: mydeploy
spec:
  replicas: 3
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: myapp
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: myapp
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: nginx
          image: nginx

MEMORY TRICK:
Deployment = ReplicaSet + rolling update

------------------------------------------------------------
6. CONFIGMAP (Stores configuration data)
------------------------------------------------------------
Template:
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: myconfig
data:
  key1: value1
  key2: value2

MEMORY TRICK:
ConfigMap = plain text config

------------------------------------------------------------
7. SECRET (Stores sensitive data - base64 encoded)
------------------------------------------------------------
Template:
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: mysecret
type: Opaque
data:
  username: dXNlcg==
  password: cGFzcw==

MEMORY TRICK:
Secret = base64 values

------------------------------------------------------------
8. NAMESPACE
------------------------------------------------------------
Template:
apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: mynamespace

MEMORY TRICK:
Smallest YAML in Kubernetes

------------------------------------------------------------
9. INGRESS (Entry point for HTTP/HTTPS)
------------------------------------------------------------
Template:
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: Ingress
metadata:
  name: myingress
spec:
  rules:
    - host: myapp.com
      http:
        paths:
          - path: /
            pathType: Prefix
            backend:
              service:
                name: myservice
                port:
                  number: 80

MEMORY TRICK:
Ingress = rules → backend service

------------------------------------------------------------
10. PERSISTENTVOLUME (PV)
------------------------------------------------------------
Template:
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolume
metadata:
  name: mypv
spec:
  capacity:
    storage: 1Gi
  accessModes:
    - ReadWriteOnce
  hostPath:
    path: /data/pv1

MEMORY TRICK:
PV = actual storage

------------------------------------------------------------
11. PERSISTENTVOLUMECLAIM (PVC)
------------------------------------------------------------
Template:
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
metadata:
  name: mypvc
spec:
  accessModes:
    - ReadWriteOnce
  resources:
    requests:
      storage: 1Gi

MEMORY TRICK:
PVC = request storage

------------------------------------------------------------
ULTIMATE MEMORY SHORTCUTS
------------------------------------------------------------
POD = containers
SERVICE = ports + selector
RC = selector + template
RS = RC (with matchLabels)
DEPLOYMENT = RS + rolling updates
CONFIGMAP = plain key-value
SECRET = base64 key-value
NAMESPACE = only metadata
INGRESS = rules + backend service
PV = defines storage
PVC = requests storage

